    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **50 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including every household-related checkpoint (Cp03, Cp10, Cp11, Cp13, Cp23, Cp25, Cp28, Cp35, Cp36).\n\n## Summary\n\nI made `householdId` deterministic and rewired duplicate detection to key off it. Three files changed:\n\n**`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 Now computes `householdId` for **every** owner as the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`, mutating the built owner in place. Removed the old opt-in gating, the cross-owner lookup, and the housemate back-fill \u2014 owners sharing last name and postcode derive the same id by construction, so no linking is needed. It no longer touches the request or repository.\n\n**`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java`** \u2014 Folded the household-duplicate block in alongside the existing identity-key check (it already runs at the right point, after `AssignHousehold`). Two rejection rules against `findAll()`:\n- Full `identityKey` match \u2192 409 (fires regardless of `sharesHousehold`, so Cp28's opted-in full duplicate still collides).\n- Same computed `householdId` as an existing owner **and** `sharesHousehold` not set \u2192 409 (household duplicate). Setting `sharesHousehold` bypasses only this block, admitting the owner as a declared member.\n\nNow takes `@Val OwnerFieldsDto request` to read the flag (that variable is already published by `ValidateOwnerFields` and consumed by many steps).\n\n**`CheckPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 Added a `differentHousehold` guard to the soft-match. Since same last-name+postcode now implies the same `householdId`, a declared household member is never flagged `possibleDuplicate` (Cp35). Any undeclared same-household owner is already rejected upstream, so the soft match only ever fires across genuinely different households.\n\n`sharesHousehold` now only bypasses the duplicate block rather than creating the link, and both duplicate detection and the identity key key off the computed `householdId`. (There is no household-size input to the membership level in this codebase \u2014 `Membership.levelOf` derives level 1\u20133 from email and namesake count only \u2014 so nothing there needed rewiring; Cp23's 3-member household resolves to level 2 as expected.)",
